{id:'cyc',cat:LIBCATS[0],ico:'calendar',t:'What to note about your cycle',min:2,src:NHSH,body:['Many clinicians ask about the date your last period started, how long your cycle usually is, how heavy it is and whether anything changed recently.','You do not need to log everything. A few consistent details (dates, flow, pain level) are more useful than a long, patchy record.','HERPATH’s cycle field is optional and can be left blank or set to “Prefer not to say”.']},
{id:'ble',cat:LIBCATS[0],ico:'drop',t:'Recording bleeding changes',min:2,src:NHSH,body:['Changes in bleeding, such as heavier flow, bleeding between periods or very irregular timing, are worth recording with dates.','Bleeding that soaks through protection very quickly, or comes with fainting or breathlessness, needs urgent medical help rather than tracking in an app.','Search the topic on the NHS or your local health service website for guidance that applies to you.']},
{id:'fat',cat:LIBCATS[1],ico:'moon',t:'Tiredness and low energy',min:2,src:NHSH,body:['Tiredness has many possible causes, so an app cannot tell you why it is happening. What helps a clinician is the pattern: how long, how often, and what it affects.','Note sleep, daily-task impact and anything that changed around the time it began.','If tiredness is persistent or worrying, speak to a healthcare professional.']},
{id:'mood',cat:LIBCATS[1],ico:'heart',t:'Mood and emotional wellbeing',min:2,src:WHO,body:['Mood changes can be linked to many things, including stress, sleep and life events. Recording how often they happen and how they affect your days can make a conversation easier.','If you have thoughts of harming yourself, please contact local emergency services or a crisis service straight away. HERPATH is not an emergency service.']},
{id:'desc',cat:LIBCATS[1],ico:'message',t:'How to describe a symptom',min:2,src:NHSH,body:['A simple structure works well: what it feels like, when it started, how long it lasts, how often it happens, how strong it is, what makes it better or worse, and what it affects.','Using the same 1–5 scale each time lets you compare entries later. It is your own rating, not a medical measurement.']},
{id:'prep',cat:LIBCATS[2],ico:'clipboard',t:'Preparing for an appointment',min:3,src:NHSH,body:['Before: choose your top two or three concerns, bring your timeline or Care Passport, and list any medicines or supplements you take.','During: say what matters most first, ask for explanations in plain language, and ask what to do if things change.','After: write down what was said while you remember it. HERPATH’s after-visit notes are for this.']},
